\ ***************************************************************************
\ STARGLIDER for the BBC Master - what the front end keeps in ANDY from
\ game to game, past the panel's: the high scores, the pilot rating's last
\ accuracy (the ST's $29E), the game's end in words, as the panel's
\ glyphs, for panel_game_over, which prints them before the front end is
\ loaded, and G's model viewer's switches. The start puts the scores and
\ the words there (start.6502).
\ ***************************************************************************

SECTION FrontAndy, org = panel_andy_end, guard = ANDY_TOP, virtual = TRUE
.hs_scores    SKIP 10 * 4   ; the best first, each BCD, its least significant byte first
.hs_names     SKIP 10 * (NAME_MAX + 1)  ; each ended by 0
.rating_pct   SKIP 1        ; the last accuracy, kept for a game with no shot fired
.go_power     SKIP GO_POWER_BYTES       ; the energy's end (mkpanel.py's GAME_OVER) ...
.go_shields   SKIP GO_SHIELDS_BYTES     ; ... and the shields'
.vw_kept_stereo SKIP 1      ; the viewer's 3 ($2CE: the start's 0) ...
.vw_kept_step SKIP 1        ; ... and P ($2CC), as the ST keeps them
.front_andy_end
ENDSECTION
